            "bug_id": 19254,
            "text": "Created attachment 3956\nFast-path exits for is() in common cases\n\n`methods::is()` is on an extremely hot path for loading S4 packages; for the set of 5 S4-heavy packages reported in Bug #19239, just loading the packages runs `is()` 358,000 times:\n\n```\nis_count <- 0\ntrace(methods::is, quote(is_count <<- is_count + 1L))\ninvisible(capture.output({\n  for (pkg in c(\"Gviz\", \"ShortRead\", \"raster\", \"timeSeries\", \"MatrixExtra\"))\n    loadNamespace(pkg)\n}))\nuntrace(methods::is)\n\nis_count\n# [1] 358085\n```\n\nThat alone consumes 4s of wall time (per `Rprof`). This patch shaves off half of that time. End-to-end, I see the `loadNamespace()` time for the 5 packages go down by over a second (19.7s -> 18.4s, about 6%).\n\nThis would also affect the proposed patch for Bug #19239, where we could switch to `is(m_class, \"MethodDefinition\") || is(m_class, \"derivedDefaultMethod\")`, which is more natural for the reader not to get caught up in `.identC()`, without much performance impact.\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/405",
            "count": 0,
            "creation_time": "2026-10-26T19:08:45Z"
          }
        ]
      }
